- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Negative findings (why this file is `.excluded`)

**ZERO verified public benchmark numbers were found for this exact model/ID.** Per the self-exclusion rule this file is saved as `GLM_5.3.md.excluded` — no scored `.md` is written, and no placeholder scores are invented.

What was verified (identity/spec metadata only, no measured accuracy numbers):

- **Identity:** GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark — a smaller version of GPT-5.3-Codex and OpenAI's "first model designed for real-time coding", launched 2026-02-12 as a **research preview** (ChatGPT Pro users in Codex; API for a small set of design partners). Also served on OpenCode Zen at `opencode/gpt-5.3-codex-spark`.
- **Speed:** more than 1000 tokens per second, served on Cerebras Wafer Scale Engine 3 — the first OpenAI model on the Cerebras low-latency path (verified: openai.com/index/introducing-gpt-5-3-codex-spark/).
- **Specs:** 128K context window and text-only input at launch (official announcement; BenchLM's tracker now lists 256K — may have been expanded since). Same safety training as mainline models; below Preparedness Framework thresholds for cyber/bio capability. Default working style deliberately lightweight: minimal targeted edits, tests not run unless asked.

Sources checked with no benchmark numbers for this ID (2026-10-01):

- BenchLM (`gpt-5-3-codex-spark`): tracked, but **0 of 618 benchmarks covered**, composite "Coming soon".
- OpenAI launch announcement: describes "strong performance" on SWE-Bench Pro and Terminal-Bench 2.0 at a fraction of GPT-5.3-Codex's duration, but all accuracy numbers are in images only — no verified values in text.
- No system card, no Artificial Analysis page, no third-party leaderboard rows found.

Interpolation from the full-size sibling GPT-5.3-Codex (SWE-bench Verified 85%, Terminal-Bench 2.0 77.3%) was deliberately NOT used to fabricate dimension scores — Spark is a different, smaller checkpoint and its accuracy is publicly unquantified. A future re-research should look for (a) published SWE-Pro / Terminal-Bench numbers for Spark, (b) a Spark system card, or (c) aggregator coverage (BenchLM/AA) once the preview graduates and multimodal/longer-context variants ship — then write a fresh `GLM_5.3.md`.

Scores inside this file are intentionally omitted/ignored: the sync skips `.excluded` files loudly.

